.TH GOODIX-MANAGER 1
.SH NAME
goodix-manager \- manage the Goodix fingerprint driver on Fedora KDE
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B goodix-manager
.SH DESCRIPTION
Opens the unprivileged Goodix Manager application. Install and update use a
verified local driver payload. PolicyKit requests administrative authorization
for changes. Removal performs the normal integrity-checked driver uninstall.
.PP
Installing or removing the Manager RPM does not activate or remove the driver.
An existing runtime retains its standalone recovery commands when the Manager
package is removed. Host pairing state and fingerprint templates are preserved.
.SH RECOVERY
Use goodix-uninstall for ordinary removal. If the desktop is unavailable or
project receipts are damaged, consult the documented goodix-force-remove TTY
procedure. These commands still require working password authentication.
.SH DOCUMENTATION
https://github.com/sorguido/goodix-27c6-5125
